outcomes:
Primary outcome: incidence of adverse events that arise during the established follow-up period, coded according to MedDRA terminology.

Exploratory outcome: Rate of non-compliance with PRAC recommendations, i.e., quantify the frequency with which patients with identified risk factors receive a prescription for Rinvoq™ despite the existence of viable therapeutic alternatives. 
Patients with risk factors are considered to be: 
(i) patients aged 65 years or older; 
(ii) current smokers or those with a long history of smoking; 
(iii) individuals at high risk of serious cardiovascular problems, such as heart attacks or strokes; 
or (iv) those more likely to develop cancer.

